+RECORDED, NO CODE CHANGE (also in HANDOFF's "Known limits")
+--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
+a. Chart Studio never writes company/cycle back, so removing a carried pill does
+   not remove the key from the URL, and loadContributions(refresh) re-carries it
+   from the URL. Idempotent - the pill comes back as it was, nothing is lost or
+   duplicated - but it does mean a removed pill can reappear on a source refresh.
+   Graph owns those two keys today; S6 may give Chart Studio ownership.
+b. scope.js merge() re-encodes unknown keys' values with encodeURIComponent, so a
+   '+' that meant a space in someone else's key is normalised to %20. Same value
+   either way under URLSearchParams decoding; harmless.
+c. A first load that names no cycle still sends latest=1 and lands on the newest
+   cycle, while the URL names no cycle at all. That is the contract's own rule
+   ("a URL names only what the reader chose") and it is unchanged from before S5,
+   but a copied link therefore means "newest", not "2024".
